@page "/demo/diagram"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared

@* 2026-10-25: new page, checked against Diagram/* (FlexCore 0.2.49). No layout engine (OffsetX/OffsetY are hand-set centers);
   no drag, zoom, editing, node keyboard or ARIA: Previous/Next are the keyboard route. Connector Ids page-unique (wf-*, sh-*):
   arrowhead marker ids are document-wide.
   2026-10-26: Previous/Next stop at the ends instead of wrapping.
   2026-11-15: text re-checked (FlexCore 0.2.50); the shapes description no longer claims every port setting.
   2026-11-15: example story moved to the Warehouse and logistics theme.
   2026-11-16: pre-deploy review fixes. *@

<PageTitle>Blazor Diagram Component — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Diagram" Category="Components" ControlName="DiagramControl"
                   Tagline="Draw a workflow or process as boxes and labeled arrows in one inline SVG."
                   SourcePath="Diagram/DiagramControl.razor;Diagram/DiagramControl.razor.css;Diagram/DiagramModels.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>DiagramControl</code> is a Blazor diagram that draws boxes and arrows, such as a receiving workflow, as one inline SVG from nodes and connectors you place. Use it to explain a process or show where a request stands; it offers six shape values (Rectangle and RoundedRectangle draw alike), straight or right-angled connectors with labels and arrowheads, and a click event for details. Users cannot drag or edit it; change the objects in C# and the diagram redraws.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="workflow" Title="A receiving workflow" RazorCode="@Code.Workflow" CSharpCode="@Code.WorkflowCs">
            <Description><p>Click a step, or use Previous step and Next step (they walk the accepted path, then the rejected branch), to read who handles it and how long it takes; the page marks the current step with a thicker outline through its <code>CssClass</code>.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="wf-layout">
                    <div class="canvas">
                        <DiagramControl Nodes="_workflowNodes" Connectors="_workflowConnectors" Width="460" Height="530"
                                        Padding="12" SizePadPercent="0" NodeClicked="OnStepClicked" />
                    </div>
                    <CardControl CssClass="wf-panel" Title="@Current.Label" Subtitle="@CurrentStep.Owner" aria-live="polite">
                        <ChildContent>
                            <dl class="wf-facts">
                                <dt>Typical time</dt>
                                <dd>@CurrentStep.Typical</dd>
                                <dt>What happens</dt>
                                <dd>@CurrentStep.Detail</dd>
                            </dl>
                        </ChildContent>
                        <FooterContent>
                            <div class="wf-buttons">
                                <ButtonControl OnClick="() => Move(-1)" Disabled="@(Index == 0)">Previous step</ButtonControl>
                                <ButtonControl OnClick="() => Move(1)" Disabled="@(Index == _workflowNodes.Count - 1)">Next step</ButtonControl>
                            </div>
                        </FooterContent>
                    </CardControl>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="shapes" Title="Shapes, connectors and links" RazorCode="@Code.Shapes" CSharpCode="@Code.ShapesCs">
            <Description><p>See every shape value and the connector styles on one canvas, with automatic ports and one connector pinned to the bottom and top. Click Bin tag scanned: the handler sets <code>Handled</code>, so its <code>NavigateUrl</code> is not followed until you switch on Follow links. Hover Bin tag scanned or Shipped for a tooltip; the gray node is disabled.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="controls">
                    <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_followLinks" Label="Follow links" />
                    <a href="demo/barcodes#barcode">Bin tag example</a>
                </div>
                <div class="canvas">
                    <DiagramControl Nodes="_shapeNodes" Connectors="_shapeConnectors" Width="550" Height="330"
                                    Padding="12" SizePadPercent="0" NodeClicked="OnShapeClicked" />
                </div>
                <p class="status" aria-live="polite">@_status</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramcontrol-parameters" Title="DiagramControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Params.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="DiagramControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Params" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramnode" Title="DiagramNode" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Node.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="DiagramNode" Rows="Vocab.Node" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramconnector" Title="DiagramConnector" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Connector.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="DiagramConnector" Rows="Vocab.Connector" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramnodeclickeventargs" Title="DiagramNodeClickEventArgs" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.ClickArgs.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="DiagramNodeClickEventArgs" Rows="Vocab.ClickArgs" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramcontrolshape" Title="DiagramControlShape" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Shapes.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="DiagramControlShape" Rows="Vocab.Shapes" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-connectortype" Title="ConnectorType" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Types.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="ConnectorType" Rows="Vocab.Types" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-diagramport" Title="DiagramPort" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Ports.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="DiagramPort" Rows="Vocab.Ports" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-arrowstyle" Title="ArrowStyle" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Arrows.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="ArrowStyle" Rows="Vocab.Arrows" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-imagefit" Title="ImageFit" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Fits.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="ImageFit" Rows="Vocab.Fits" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-variables" Title="CSS variables" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Vars.Length, "variables")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssVariables" Title="CSS variables" Rows="Vocab.Vars" />
                <p>Fill, outline and text colors come from the node and connector properties, not from CSS variables.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>Labels, sublabels, icons and connector labels are SVG <code>&lt;text&gt;</code> elements: real text, not pictures of text.</li>
            <li>A node's <code>Tooltip</code> becomes an SVG <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, the first child of the node's group; browsers show it on hover.</li>
            <li>Give every node action a second route that works from the keyboard. In the first example, Previous step and Next step walk every step, and the card that describes the step is an <code>aria-live="polite"</code> region. In the second, the Bin tag example link beside the canvas goes where Bin tag scanned leads.</li>
            <li>To name the diagram, wrap it in a <code>&lt;figure&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;</code>, or put a heading just before it.</li>
            <li>A disabled node is drawn at 45% opacity with a close icon and ignores clicks. When that state matters, say it in the node's <code>Label</code> or <code>SubLabel</code> as well.</li>
            <li>Pick <code>FillColor</code> and <code>TextColor</code> with at least 4.5:1 contrast, and leave some margin for sublabels, which are drawn at 85% opacity.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Tasks with dependency links on a timeline: <a href="demo/gantt">Gantt chart</a>.</li>
            <li>Hierarchies as an expandable list: <a href="demo/tree/treeview-explorer">Tree view</a>.</li>
            <li>The bin tag the second example links to: <a href="demo/barcodes#barcode">Barcodes &amp; QR</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

@code {
    // Workflow
    private sealed record Step(string Owner, string Typical, string Detail);

    private static readonly Dictionary<string, Step> Steps = new()
    {
